38. execute_schedule_dispatch(shift_candidate_alpha, vehicle_unit_gamma, dispatch_slot_alpha)
39. release_operator_resource(shift_candidate_alpha, driver_operator_alpha)
40. release_skill_certificate(shift_candidate_alpha, skill_certificate_alpha)
41. release_compliance_certificate(shift_candidate_alpha, compliance_certificate_alpha)
42. create_candidate(shift_candidate_beta)
43. allocate_vehicle_unit(shift_candidate_beta, vehicle_unit_alpha)   ; vehicle alpha now free after origin dispatch
44. attach_task_profile(shift_candidate_beta, route_task_profile_alpha)
45. confirm_candidate_preparedness(shift_candidate_beta, route_task_profile_alpha)
46. assign_operator_resource(shift_candidate_beta, driver_operator_alpha)
47. assign_skill_certificate(shift_candidate_beta, skill_certificate_alpha)
48. assign_compliance_certificate(shift_candidate_beta, compliance_certificate_alpha)
49. load_container_onto_leg(shift_candidate_beta, loading_container_beta, transport_leg_alpha)
50. stage_schedule_candidate(shift_candidate_beta, loading_container_beta, transport_leg_alpha, route_task_profile_alpha)
51. verify_loading_profile_nominal(shift_candidate_beta, skill_certificate_alpha, driver_operator_alpha, loading_container_beta, transport_leg_alpha)
52. establish_clearance_nominal(shift_candidate_beta, compliance_certificate_alpha, loading_container_beta, transport_leg_alpha)
53. finalize_candidate_direct(shift_candidate_beta)
54. allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate(shift_candidate_beta, dispatch_slot_alpha, route_task_profile_alpha)
55. execute_schedule_dispatch(shift_candidate_beta, vehicle_unit_alpha, dispatch_slot_alpha)
56. release_operator_resource(shift_candidate_beta, driver_operator_alpha)
57. release_skill_certificate(shift_candidate_beta, skill_certificate_alpha)
58. release_compliance_certificate(shift_candidate_beta, compliance_certificate_alpha)

Now we have all four dispatched.

Check that after step 21 execute_origin_dispatch, we released vehicle_unit_alpha and dispatch_slot_alpha. Good.

Step 24 execute_destination_dispatch releases vehicle_unit_beta and dispatch_slot_alpha.

Thus after step 24, vehicle_unit_alpha and beta are available, dispatch slot available.

Now step 25 create shift alpha, step 26 allocate vehicle_unit_gamma (available). Good.

After step 38 execute_schedule_dispatch for alpha, vehicle_unit_gamma becomes available, dispatch slot available.

Now step 43 allocate vehicle_unit_alpha for beta (available). Good.

After step 55 execute schedule dispatch for beta, vehicle_unit_alpha becomes available, dispatch slot available.

Now we need to verify that we didn't violate any precondition like candidate_prepared before assign_operator_resource. We did confirm_candidate_preparedness before assign_operator_resource for origin/destination and schedule candidates. Good.

Now we need to verify that after we allocated vehicle unit and attached task profile, we have candidate_task_profile_linked true; confirm_candidate_preparedness requires that.

Now we need to verify that after we assigned operator, we have candidate_operator_linked true; lock_origin_availability requires candidate_operator_linked (we have after assign). Good.

Now we need to verify that after we released operator from origin and destination, we still have candidate_operator_linked? The release_operator_resource effect removes candidate_operator_linked and makes operator_available. So after release, candidate_operator_linked is false. Does lock_origin_availability require candidate_operator_linked? Yes, its precondition includes candidate_operator_linked. So we must release operator after locking, not before. We released after lock, which is fine because lock already succeeded.

Now after we released operator, candidate_operator_linked becomes false. Does any later action require candidate_operator_linked for origin/destination? For mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready, we need origin_availability_locked and origin_availability_confirmed, transport_leg_assembled, transport_leg_loading_authorized, not dispatch_ready. No operator needed. For execute_origin_dispatch we need candidate_vehicle_linked and candidate_dispatch_slot_linked, not operator. So fine.

Now for destination similar.

Now for schedule candidates, we need operator for assign_operator_resource (precondition candidate_prepared). We assigned operator after confirm_candidate_preparedness. After that we never need operator again except for release later. The loading verification etc does not require operator? Actually verify_loading_profile_nominal requires candidate_operator_linked (yes). So we need operator linked during verification and clearance establishment. So we must keep operator linked until after establish_clearance_nominal? Actually verify_loading_profile_nominal requires candidate_operator_linked. establish_clearance_nominal does not require operator. So we need operator linked at least until verify_loading_profile_nominal. After that we can release operator before finalize? finalize_candidate_direct does not require operator. So we can release operator after verify or after establish. In our plan we released after execute_schedule_dispatch, which is after finalize, allocate, execute. That's okay because operator remains linked through verify, establish, finalize, allocate, execute. No action requires operator after verify, so it's fine.

Now we need to check that we didn't accidentally use the same skill certificate for both candidates without releasing in between. We released after alpha dispatch, before beta's assign. Good.

Now compliance certificate similarly.

Now we need to verify that we didn't accidentally use the same loading container for both candidates without releasing? Loading container is not released by any action; loading_container_loaded remains true after load. There is no action to unload container from leg. However we might not need to unload; it's okay if container stays loaded. No further actions require loading_container_available for anything else. So fine.

Now we need to verify that we didn't accidentally use the same transport leg for multiple loads; loading_container_leg_linked can be true for multiple containers; no conflict.

Now we need to verify that we didn't accidentally set any negative precondition that later becomes true causing conflict. For example, after we load container onto leg for alpha, we have loading_container_loaded true for alpha. This does not affect any precondition that requires not loading_container_loaded for something else, except load_container_onto_leg for beta requires not loading_container_loaded for beta's container, which is fine.

Now we need to verify that we didn't accidentally set origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded true inadvertently. We never performed actions that set those: assemble_origin_loaded_leg, assemble_destination_loaded_leg, assemble_fully_loaded_leg. We only used assemble_transport_leg and load_container_onto_leg. Those do not set origin_leg_loaded or destination_leg_loaded. So they remain false.

Now we need to verify that we didn't accidentally set route_sequence_context_set true; we never used actions that set it (establish_clearance_origin_loaded, establish_clearance_destination_loaded, establish_clearance_full_load). So it's false.

Now we need to verify that we didn't accidentally set candidate_finalized true before we intend; we only set via finalize_candidate_direct after clearance established, which is correct.

Now we need to verify that we didn't accidentally set dispatch_ready true for schedule candidates before allocating dispatch slot; we set via finalize_candidate_direct, then allocate slot, then execute. Good.

Now we need to verify that we didn't accidentally set dispatch_allocated true for origin/destination before marking dispatch ready; we allocated after marking ready. Good.

Now we need to verify that we didn't allocate dispatch slot before marking dispatch ready; we allocated after marking ready.

Now we need to verify that we didn't allocate vehicle unit after we already had it allocated; we allocate before attach task profile, which is fine.

Now we need to verify that we didn't allocate vehicle unit for origin after we already allocated it for something else; we used distinct.

Now we need to verify that we didn't allocate vehicle unit for destination after we already allocated it for origin; we used beta.

Now we need to verify that we didn't allocate vehicle unit for schedule alpha after we allocated it for origin/destination; we used gamma.

Now we need to verify that we didn't allocate vehicle unit for schedule beta after we allocated it for origin/destination/alpha schedule; we used alpha after origin dispatch released it.

Now we need to verify that we didn't use any action that requires something we have not yet established.

Let's go through each step and check preconditions.

